<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Germany</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as German</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Germany is a country in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>. Its lands formed the core of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a> and were unified in 1871 as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a>. Germany was the ally of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austria-Hungary</a> and later of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> in the world wars, and it figures in the histories of the Carolingian, Spanish and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swedish-empire">Swedish Empires</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/germany.jpg" alt="Germany" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SKopp, Madden, and other users · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Germany.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The French word for <b>Germany</b>, Allemagne, and the Spanish Alemania come from the Alemanni, one people of the south-west, not from the Germans as a whole.</blockquote><a href="/empire/alemanni">Alemanni · At a glance</a></li><li><blockquote>Argentina remained neutral in both world wars until it declared war on <b>Germany</b> and Japan in March 1945.</blockquote><a href="/empire/argentine-republic">Argentine Republic · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Austrian predominance in <b>Germany</b> and Italy delayed both national unifications, which when they came were achieved against Austria.</blockquote><a href="/empire/austrian-empire">Austrian Empire · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>The Brusilov Offensive of 1916 broke the Habsburg army as an independent fighting force, and thereafter the empire was increasingly a junior partner to <b>Germany</b>.</blockquote><a href="/empire/austro-hungarian-empire">Austro-Hungarian Empire · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1940 Britain demilitarised the island, which <b>Germany</b> then fortified as part of the Atlantic Wall.</blockquote><a href="/empire/bailiwick-of-jersey">Bailiwick of Jersey · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>In 936 Abd al-Rahman III began building the palace city of Madinat al-Zahra west of Córdoba, where foreign envoys, among them embassies from Byzantium and from Otto I of <b>Germany</b>, were received with elaborate ritual.</blockquote><a href="/empire/caliphate-of-cordoba">Caliphate of Córdoba · Governance &amp; Law</a></li></ul></section>
